107 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 48 0 R/E(Breath work is integral to yoga and all round wellbeing, practice these breathing Pranayama techniques to help you calm and centre during practice and generally.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

108 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 48 0 R/E(\200 Long deep breathing)/Pg 14 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

109 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 48 0 R/E(The benefits of long deep breathing include relaxation, stress release, stimulation of endorphins that fight depression, expansion of lung capacity and an increase in patience. Start by closing the eyes, relaxing the breath and smoothly breathe through the nose. Notice the movement of the abdomen and allow the abdomen to expand. As the slow, deep inhalation is continued, the rib cage and upper chest will also expand. The breath moves into the body like a glass fills with water filling from the lower lungs upwards. Exhale the breath out as a glass would empty, pouring it out from the upper chest, then ribcage, and finally drawing the navel in towards the spine.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

110 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 48 0 R/E(\200 Ujjayi breath)/Pg 14 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

111 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 48 0 R/E(Holding one hand just in front of the mouth, inhale a deep breath through the nose while holding the hand in front of the mouth and then open the mouth and exhale the breath through the mouth, creating a \217haaaaaah\220 sound. Imagine that the hand is a mirror and that the breath is fogging up the mirror. Now inhale again and on the exhale keep the mouth closed, breathing through the nose. Try to make the same sound as when the mouth was open.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

112 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 48 0 R/E(The sounds made during this breathing technique are similar to the sounds of the ocean, which is why this breathing technique is also known as \217oceans breathe\220.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

113 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 48 0 R/E(\200 Golden thread breath)/Pg 14 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

114 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 48 0 R/E(It\220s called Golden Thread Breath because it\220s like blowing a golden thread from your lips gently into the distance or like a fine golden breath spinning out between the lips.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

115 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 48 0 R/E(Start by ensuring that your face and jaw are completely relaxed, teeth and lips very slightly apart. Take a deep breath in through the nose, imagining breathing in energy and oxygen into your body and your baby, then a really slow, gentle, controlled breath out through your mouth.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

