<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 55 0 R/T(Flying from the floor \(Horsey Horsey\))/E(Flying from the floor \(Horsey Horsey\))/Pg 21 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

240 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 55 0 R/T(From semi supine press your lower back into the ground. Lift the legs into a right angle position with the knees over the hips and contract the abdominal muscles. Place your baby\220s face down onto your lower legs \(baby\220s head near mothers knees\), which at this point are level to the ground. Hold your baby on your legs \(under the arms tends to work best\) and slowly lower your feet part way to the ground, keeping the thighs perpendicular to the ground. Repeat several times as you sing the song \215Horsey Horsey\216.)/E(From semi supine press your lower back into the ground. Lift the legs into a right angle position with the knees over the hips and contract the abdominal muscles. Place your baby\220s face down onto your lower legs \(baby\220s head near mothers knees\), which at this point are level to the ground. Hold your baby on your legs \(under the arms tends to work best\) and slowly lower your feet part way to the ground, keeping the thighs perpendicular to the ground. Repeat several times as you sing the song \215Horsey Horsey\216.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

